unittest so regressions in tokenizer or tie-break fail loudly. Why: the tokenizer regex and sort key are the only subtle logic in the package. Write tests/test_core.py (currently empty) using unittest.TestCase, importing from textstats.core (import word_count, unique_words, top_words, _tokenize as needed). Add `if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\": unittest.main()` at the bottom. Required cases: word_count(\\\"The cat. The dog!\\\") == 4; unique_words(\\\"The the THE\\\") == 1; word_count(\\\"don't stop\\\") == 2 and word_count(\\\"don't\\\") == 1; top_words(\\\"b a b a c\\\", 2) == [(\\\"a\\\", 2), (\\\"b\\\", 2)]; top_words(\\\"x\\\", 5) == [(\\\"x\\\", 1)]; top_words(\\\"x y\\\", 0) == []; word_count(\\\"\\\") == 0, unique_words(\\\"\\\") == 0, top_words(\\\"\\\", 3) == []; underscores dropped (word_count(\\\"a_b\\\") == 0? NO: \\\"a_b\\\" tokenizes to [\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"], so assert 2); digits kept (word_count(\\\"room 101\\\") == 2); case-insensitive top_words(\\\"A a\\\", 1) == [(\\\"a\\\", 2)]. Ruled out: changing textstats/core.py (owned by i3; if a test fails, report it, do not edit core), third-party test libs, pytest-only features (use unittest only).\" :bar \"Running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_core.py` from repo root exits 0 and reports at least 10 tests run with OK, covering: word_count of \\\"The cat. The dog!\\\" is 4; unique_words of \\\"The the THE\\\" is 1; \\\"don't stop\\\" gives 2 tokens and \\\"don't\\\" gives 1; top_words of \\\"x\\\" with n=5 is [(\\\"x\\\", 1)]; top_words of \\\"x y\\\" with n=0 is []; empty string gives 0, 0, [].\" :casts 1)\n(ingot :id \"i5\" :status ore :solo nil :grade 2 :skill cli :heat 0 :max 5 :smelt 0 :proof \"python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md | grep -qE '^words: [0-9]+$' && python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md | grep -qE '^unique: [0-9]+$' && python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md | grep -qE '^top: ' && python3 -m py_compile textstats/cli.py\" :work \"Goal: a thin CLI over core. Why: this is the user-visible deli