tly against the expected string including trailing newlines. Cases: (a) 'the cat sat on the mat' file -> stdout 'words: 6\\\\nunique: 5\\\\ntop: the=2, cat=1, mat=1, on=1, sat=1\\\\n', return 0; (b) empty file -> stdout 'words: 0\\\\nunique: 0\\\\ntop:\\\\n', return 0; (c) nonexistent path inside temp dir -> return 1, stderr starts with 'error: cannot read'; (d) main([]) -> return 2, stderr contains 'usage'. Add `if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\": unittest.main()`. Ruled out: subprocess calls, editing cli.py (owned by i5; if a case fails, report exact output, do not edit cli.py), pytest, writing files outside the temp directory.\" :bar \"Running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_cli.py` from repo root exits 0 and reports OK with at least 4 tests, covering: a temp file containing `the cat sat on the mat` prints exactly the three lines `words: 6`, `unique: 5`, `top: the=2, cat=1, mat=1, on=1, sat=1`; an empty file prints `words: 0`, `unique: 0`, `top:` with no trailing space; a missing path returns 1 with an `error:` line on stderr; no argument returns 2 with usage on stderr.\" :casts 1)\n(ingot :id \"i7\" :status ore :solo nil :grade 1 :skill default :heat 0 :max 5 :smelt 0 :proof \"test -f README.md && grep -q 'python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md' README.md && grep -q 'python3 -m unittest discover -s tests' README.md && grep -q '^top: ' README.md\" :work \"Goal: a one-example README that is accurate. Why: users copy the example; it must match real output. Create README.md at repo root (currently absent). Use PRD.md as the example input (decision: it already exists; do NOT create notes.txt or any new data file). Step 1: run `python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md` from repo root and capture its exact stdout. Step 2: write README.md with: a one-paragraph description of textstats (stdlib-only Python package counting words, unique words, and top 5 words, case-insensitive); a usage section with a fenced shell block `python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md` and a fenced output block containing the captured three lines verbatim; a tests section with a fenced block `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` run from repo root. Ruled out: extra examples, badges, install instructions, setup.py, any file other than README.md. Do not hand-type the output; paste the captured output. No comments in any file.\" :bar \"README.md at repo root contains one descriptive paragraph, one usage example block showing `python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md` followed by the exact three-line output that the command prints when run from repo root, and a line showing `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`; the example output matches the live CLI output byte-for-byte.\" :casts 1)\n(ingot :id \"i8\" :status ore :solo nil :grade 1 :skill default :heat 0 :max 5 :smelt 0 :proof \"python3 -m py_compile textstats/*.py tests/*.py && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests && python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md > /tmp/ts_run1.txt && python3 -m textstats.cli PRD.md > /tmp/ts_run2.txt && diff /tmp/ts_run1.txt /tmp/ts_run2.txt && ! grep -rqE '^(import|from) (numpy|requests|pytest|yaml|click)' textstats tests\" :work \"Goal: final gate for the whole package. Why: confirms the blueprint acceptance criteria hold together. Do NOT edit any file in this ingot; it is verification only. Run the proof command exactly. If any step fails, do not patch: report the failing command and its full output. Also run `git status --short` and confirm .cfg/ and .terminal.log are unchanged and no .env file was created or modified. Ruled out: committing, editing files, adding new tests. Report the three-line CLI output on PRD.md in the final summary.\" :bar \"From repo root: all package and test files compile under py_compile; full discover run exits 0; two consecutive CLI runs on PRD.md produce byte-identical output; and no third-party imports appear in textstats or tests. Also `git status --short` shows no change to .cfg/ or .terminal.log.\" :casts 1)\n"}
