# Tiny word frequency

Requires Node.js 18 or newer; no dependencies.

```sh
node cli.js --help
node cli.js --top 3 fixtures/sample.txt
printf 'apple banana apple\n' | node cli.js
node --test
```

Supply one UTF-8 file path, or omit it to read stdin. `--top N` selects a
positive integer limit (default: 10). Output is one `word count` per line,
ordered by descending count, then word for ties. Words are case-insensitive
Unicode letter/number sequences; punctuation separates words. Empty input
produces no output. Use `--` before a path beginning with a dash.

The package bin entry `word-frequency` targets `cli.js`; the direct launch
command is `node cli.js`. Tests verify this metadata and invoke the real CLI
with read-only fixtures and in-memory stdin.
