# Local utility

a small Python CLI that converts CSV to JSON with a --pretty flag, in a package with tests

## CHECKLIST
- [ ] Convert CSV with a header row into a JSON array of objects keyed by column names, preserving cell values as strings; commit tests/fixtures/sample.csv with representative input.
- [ ] The installed csv-to-json command accepts a CSV file path and prints valid JSON to stdout; when no file is given, it reads CSV from stdin.
- [ ] The --pretty flag prints indented, multiline JSON with the same parsed content as the default output.
- [ ] The --help flag prints usage documenting the optional input path, stdin behavior, and --pretty, then exits successfully.
- [ ] Provide installation metadata for an importable Python package with a csv-to-json console-script entry point.
- [ ] Provide unittest tests for conversion and subprocess assertions for file input, stdin, --pretty, and --help; tests run without filesystem writes using in-memory data or committed fixtures.
- [ ] Include installation metadata and importable modules for the requested package. Document its intended installation and launch or import commands.
- [ ] Run the stated CLI launch and --help. Use subprocess checks that assert actual results for the named behavior and flags.
- [ ] Run a nonempty full test suite that exercises the commission's named behavior.
- [ ] Provide a console-script entry point for the package CLI. Install in a local virtual environment before review. Document and run its installed console command.
- [ ] Read stdin when no input file is given. Document this interface and --help. Run stdin and help probes, and test their results through the real CLI.

