# tiny-wordfreq

Requires Node.js 18 or newer; no installation or dependencies needed.

```sh
node bin/wordfreq.js -n 2 fixtures/sample.txt
node bin/wordfreq.js --help
printf 'apple banana apple\n' | node bin/wordfreq.js
node --test
```

Pass one text-file path, or omit it to read stdin. `-n N` selects a positive
integer maximum (default **10**). Fewer distinct words produce fewer rows.
Output is `word<TAB>count`, one row per word, highest count first; ties sort
alphabetically. Words are lowercased Unicode letter/digit sequences;
punctuation separates words. Empty input produces no rows. Invalid arguments
and unreadable files report errors on stderr and exit nonzero.
Use `--` before a file path beginning with a dash.

The package's `bin` entry maps `wordfreq` to `bin/wordfreq.js`.
Tests verify this mapping and exercise that CLI directly through Node.


